  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "What this page shows",
      "description": "Reading guide: what the panels measure, the 60-second sample interval, the 15-day retention, and why the dashboard time range has to cover the capture.",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 11,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "ci-observe-metrics"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "**One capture, minute by minute.** Pick a run in the **Run** box, then read top to bottom: how many pods existed, what each pod used in CPU and memory, what the node used, and the table of every pod with its first and last sample.\n\n**Samples are 60 seconds.** The collector scrapes the kubelet summary API once a minute, so one point is one minute and the charts cannot show anything faster. Prometheus keeps **15 days** of samples.\n\n**The time range must cover the capture.** A finished capture has no samples in \"now\", so a range that ends before the capture starts, or begins after it ends, renders empty. Set the range to the capture's start and end, or a little wider. The page opens on the last 24 hours, which covers today's runs at close to the real one-minute resolution.\n\n**The table keeps working after the capture ends; a plain instant query does not.** The table reads its values with range functions over the dashboard range (`max_over_time(...[$__range])`), so a finished capture still renders it. A bare instant query of a metric stops returning anything about **five minutes** after the last sample: that is Prometheus's lookback window, not missing data.\n\nThe pod series carry no node label, so this page cannot say which node a pod ran on. Node metrics are cluster-wide: one line per node."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Pod count",
      "description": "Number of distinct pods that reported a CPU sample at each 60-second step. Counted from k8s_pod_cpu_usage, so a pod that exists but reports no CPU sample is not counted. A gap means no samples were collected in that minute, not an empty cluster.",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "ci-observe-metrics"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "axisLabel": "",
            "scaleDistribution": {
              "type": "linear"
            },
            "hideFrom": {
              "legend": false,
              "tooltip": false,
              "viz": false
            },
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "off"
            }
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "noValue": "No pod samples in this range"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "max",
            "last"
          ],
          "showLegend": true
