    {
      "id": 7,
      "title": "Pods seen",
      "description": "Every pod that produced any sample during the dashboard time range, with its namespace, its first and last sample time, and its peak CPU and peak memory. This is the answer to 'which pods existed, and when': a pod whose first sample is late was created late, and a pod whose last sample is early was deleted early. The sample times come from the pod working-set metric, which every scraped pod reports. A blank Peak CPU means the pod has no CPU sample: CPU usage is a rate, so a pod scraped only once cannot have one. There is no node column because the pod series carry no node label.",
